# The diagnostic for `parallel for` over the three-clause loop form, locked
# byte-for-byte as tests/diag/parallel_three_clause.err. Refused at
# src/tychoc.c:3465, whose text names both forms `parallel` DOES support.
#
# Why this fixture exists: tests/reject/*.ty asserts only a nonzero exit and a
# non-empty diagnostic (see the reject loop in tests/run.sh), so this message
# could degrade to "syntax error" and every lane would stay green. It was
# verified by reading the source once, which is the check that does not survive
# the next edit. This is the same discipline as tests/diag/dotlt_sequential.err,
# which pins the message a user hits coming the other way.
fn main():
    total := 0
    parallel for i := 0; i < 3; i += 1:
        total += i
    print(str(total))
